---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig, withBase } from '../config/site';
import { ArrowUpRight } from 'lucide-static';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Download"
  description="Download the current Daena Archive alpha from GitHub Releases and review release-specific platform requirements."
>
  <header class="download-hero dark-panel">
    <div class="content-shell download-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Alpha · v0.1.0</span><h1 class="page-heading">
          Open the archive carefully.
        </h1><p class="lede">
          Daena is in active early development and is not production ready. The release page is the
          single source for currently published builds, installation requirements, and known
          limitations.
        </p><div class="button-row">
          <a class="button button-brass" href={siteConfig.releases}>View GitHub Releases <span set:html={ArrowUpRight}></span></a><a
            class="button button-secondary"
            href={withBase('/docs/getting-started/installing-daena/')}>Installation guide</a
          >
        </div>
      </div><div class="download-seal" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>α</span><i></i><b>DAENA ARCHIVE</b>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="content-shell download-notes">
      <article>
        <span>01</span><h2>Check the release notes</h2><p>
          Platform builds and package formats can change during alpha. The website does not
          duplicate a platform matrix that could become stale.
        </p>
      </article><article>
        <span>02</span><h2>Back up important projects</h2><p>
          Keep a separate copy of project folders you care about and read migration notes before
          opening them with a new alpha build.
        </p>
      </article><article>
        <span>03</span><h2>Report what you find</h2><p>
          Reproducible bug reports and focused contributions help turn the alpha into a dependable
          first beta.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="release-authority">
    <div class="reading-shell">
      <span class="eyebrow">Current authority</span><h2>Why no platform buttons here?</h2><p>
        {siteConfig.platforms}
      </p><p>
        A conventional download grid would look convenient while quietly becoming incorrect. GitHub
        Releases stays closest to the artifacts, checksums, and per-release notes.
      </p><div class="button-row">
        <a class="button button-primary" href={siteConfig.releases}>Open releases</a><a
          class="text-link"
          href={siteConfig.issues}>Report an issue</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .download-hero {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
  }
  .download-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
    gap: 5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .download-hero .lede {
    color: #b8b1a5;
  }
  .download-hero .button-secondary {
    border-color: #45584d;
    background: transparent;
    color: #f2eee4;
  }
  .download-seal {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 24rem;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border: 1px solid #42574b;
    border-radius: var(--radius-large);
  }
  .download-seal::before,
  .download-seal::after {
    position: absolute;
    width: 17rem;
    height: 17rem;
    border: 1px solid #4b604f;
    border-radius: 50%;
    content: '';
  }
  .download-seal::after {
    width: 10rem;
    height: 10rem;
    border-color: #b48143;
    border-style: dashed;
  }
  .download-seal span {
    z-index: 2;
    color: #e4c786;
    font: italic 7rem var(--font-serif);
  }
  .download-seal i {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 100%;
    background: #42574b;
  }
  .download-seal b {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 1.2rem;
    color: #aaa296;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  }
  .download-notes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
  }
  .download-notes article {
    padding: 2rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .download-notes article:last-child {
    border-right: 0;
  }
  .download-notes span {
    color: var(--copper-text);
    font: italic 1rem var(--font-serif);
  }
  .download-notes h2 {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.7rem;
  }
  .download-notes p {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  .release-authority {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: var(--paper-warm);
  }
  .release-authority h2 {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .release-authority p {
    margin-top: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 55rem) {
    .download-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .download-seal {
      min-height: 17rem;
    }
    .download-notes {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .download-notes article {
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .download-notes article:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
